WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:05.500
In non-technical subjects like history, literature, and science, students shouldn't outsource their thinking to AI.

2
00:05.500 --> 00:09.500
That's why we created the Socratic Split-Screen.

3
00:09.500 --> 00:16.000
On the left is My Brain: a distraction-free writing editor. On the right is the Socratic AI Tutor, initially locked behind a padlock.

4
00:16.000 --> 00:22.500
The AI remains grayed out until the student drafts at least two hundred words of their own authentic thought.

5
00:22.500 --> 00:28.000
Once unlocked, the AI is strictly forbidden from writing essays or handing out direct answers.

6
00:28.000 --> 00:36.000
Instead, it acts as a classical mentor: probing for blind spots, questioning structural assumptions, and guiding the student to master critical thinking.

